Decided: `shed events --machine` passes lines that are not events (`reset`, `lagged`, the blank line before `lagged`) through unchanged; only real events get the machine prefix or the linked filter.
Because: crates/shed/src/main.rs:773
Rejected: skipping non-event lines — the client would never see that it lagged or that its `since` was reset, which is the point of those notices.
Decided: heartbeats are opt-in per connection; the ACP bridge writer and machine links opt in.
Because: "A heartbeat every 15 s in both directions; a peer that misses 2 is dropped."
Rejected: enforcing heartbeats on every connection — `shed events`, attach, watch and outside clients send nothing after their request and would be cut off after 30 s.
Decided: a subscriber more than 4,096 events behind is closed with a `lagged` line; a `since` older than the ring gets a `reset` line first.
Because: "A subscriber more than N events behind is dropped with a `lagged` notice, and it resumes with `since` or gets a reset."
Decided: main ring 4,096 non-text events; text in a 256-chunk ring per terminal.
